    => SAFE (margin>0), supports the claim

[5] HASKELL LENS: curry ev at witness t* ⇒ tournament arcs = sign Im χ_{v_a-v_b}(t*)
    S=[1, 2, 3, 5, 8], witness t*=0.27275, G=0.1818, δ=0.1667
    arcs (a→b if Im e^{2πi(v_a−v_b)t*}>0), indexed by difference set S−S:
    out-degrees (tournament score seq): [1, 2, 2, 2, 3]
    #arcs=10 (of 10 pairs); difference set size |S−S|=15

[6] THETA-FUNCTION form  good-measure = Σ_{m∈Λ=ker(v)} Π ĝ(m_i)
    Lemma A = 'the relation-lattice theta sum is dominated by its constant term'
    config        | (1-2δ)^k const | corrections | const+corr | actual good | λ1(Λ)=min relation
    circuit-free  | 0.1328         | -0.0339     | 0.0989     | 0.1071      | 4
    {1..6} (AP)   | 0.1328         | -0.0551     | 0.0778     | 0.0000      | 3
    {7..12} (AP↑) | 0.1328         | -0.0015     | 0.1313     | 0.1404      | 4
    geometric     | 0.1328         | +0.0831     | 0.2159     | 0.2319      | 3
    => circuit-free: corrections ≈ 0, theta ≈ const > 0 (Lemma A); AP {1..6}: large negative
       corrections cancel the const → good=0 (tight). λ1(Λ) small = short 3-term relation.

[7] AP-TRANSLATION FLIP: {m+1..m+k} keeps additive energy but kills 3-term relations
    m | set          | energy | 3term | G-δ      | regime
    0 | [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6]|  146   |   9   | -0.0000 | TIGHT (Lemma B)
    2 | [3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8]|  146   |   4   | +0.1298 | safe (Lemma A)
    4 | [5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10]|  146   |   1   | +0.1904 | safe (Lemma A)
    6 | [7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12]|  146   |   0   | +0.2253 | safe (Lemma A)
    8 | [9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14]|  146   |   0   | +0.2482 | safe (Lemma A)
    => energy constant (translation-invariant); 3-term count drops to 0 once m≥k;
       the gap flips TIGHT→safe exactly when the 3-term relations vanish.
